          "Conditional sentences type III (if + past perfect, main clause with would + have + past participle) refer to imaginary situations in the past: e.g. If I had had enough money, I would have bought a Ferrari.",
          "The if-clause can come first (with a comma) or second (without a comma): I would ring the police if I saw a burglar breaking into my house.",
          "In type II we can use were with I / he / she / it: If I weren't in debt, I would quit my job.",
