          "wish + could + infinitive = a wish about the present or future ability: I can't watch the match tonight. I wish I could watch it.",
          "wish + would + infinitive = a strong desire that someone does something or changes (present or future): I wish our head teacher would limit absence in our school.",
          "If only has the same meaning as I wish, but it is stronger: If only they had asked you for help before they started.",
